{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"N198\",\"lines\":\"n-rn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N198.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"ءَامَنُوٓا۟\",\"after\":\"Believers’ trust is heard beside the hand as a shelter.\",\"reason\":\"The target is سكون القلب في أمن وثقة, while the rare اليد is إياد, a حاجز يحفظ الشيء. Protection can produce security, but this is a broad causal echo.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N198.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The washed hands also appear as the body’s guarding limbs.\",\"reason\":\"وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ names bodily hands, while إياد is a حاجز that preserves what it guards. The cleansing command lets the hands be pictured as protectors turned toward prayer.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N198.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"جُنُبًا\",\"after\":\"The state of bodily distance is heard beside a protective flank.\",\"reason\":\"جُنُبًا is glossed as a bodily side or adjacent region, while the rare إياد is a حاجز that guards. A side and its protective barrier make a possible but thin bodily image.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N199\",\"lines\":\"-rn----rr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N199.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The hands washed for prayer are also heard as hands that give.\",\"reason\":\"The target وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ is the bodily hand, and اليد can name النعمة والإحسان, generosity and benefaction. The ritual organ becomes the image of a giving hand within an ayah that later names God’s favor.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N199.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْمَرَافِقِ\",\"after\":\"The favoring hand echoes the elbow’s gentleness.\",\"reason\":\"The rare اليد is الإحسان, a freely given kindness, and ٱلْمَرَافِقِ carries اللين ولطافة الفعل, gentle and skillful conduct. Both point toward benevolence, though the elbow boundary keeps the pairing broad.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N199.8\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"نِعْمَتَهُۥ\",\"after\":\"The hand’s gift is named again as favor completed upon the believers.\",\"reason\":\"The rare hand-sense is اليد النعمة والإحسان, a blessing or benefaction, and نِعْمَتَهُۥ is حسن الحال والنعمة, favor and good condition. The paired words let the bodily purification sit inside a gift that God completes.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N199.9\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"تَشْكُرُونَ\",\"after\":\"A gift from the hand calls forth the community’s gratitude.\",\"reason\":\"The rare hand is the giver of اليَد النعمة, whereas تَشْكُرُونَ means recognizing النعمة and praising its giver. Giving and grateful recognition form the response-and-reception pair that closes the ayah.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N200\",\"lines\":\"n----\"}\n{\"id\":\"N200.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The washed hand is heard as the hand in which something is held.\",\"reason\":\"The target is the bodily اليَد, while the rare phrase الشيء في يدي means that a thing is in one’s possession. The hand under the washing command can faintly carry the image of an organ that holds and controls.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N201\",\"lines\":\"-n------\"}\n{\"id\":\"N201.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The bodily hand carries a faint resonance of authority.\",\"reason\":\"The ordinary hand gloss includes اليَد القوّة, strength, while the rare اليَد السلطان means authority and effective command. Power overlaps, but the ayah’s hands are bodily organs, so the sovereignty echo remains thin.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N202\",\"lines\":\"r-rn--n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N202.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"ءَامَنُوٓا۟\",\"after\":\"Faith appears as trust enacted through obedience.\",\"reason\":\"The rare hand is الطاعة والاستسلام, obedience and surrender, and ءَامَنُوٓا۟ is سكون القلب في أمن وثقة, trustful security. The opening address joins inward trust to the bodily acts commanded here.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N202.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The hands themselves become an image of obedience.\",\"reason\":\"وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ names the bodily hand, while اليد can mean الطاعة والاستسلام, submission and obedience. As those hands are washed and wiped, compliance takes visible bodily form.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N202.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱمْسَحُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The act of wiping can be heard as a gesture of surrender.\",\"reason\":\"The rare اليد means الطاعة, obedience, and وَٱمْسَحُوا۟ commands passing the hand over a surface. The commanded motion can enact submission, though that reading is a general one.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N202.7\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱمْسَحُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The substitute wipe remains an act of obedient surrender.\",\"reason\":\"The rare hand-sense is الاستسلام, surrender, and فَٱمْسَحُوا۟ gives the wiping instruction for the earth rite. The reduced-contact gesture can still be heard as compliance with the command.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N203\",\"lines\":\"-n-n--rr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N203.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The bodily hand faintly recalls what passes from hand to hand.\",\"reason\":\"The target is the physical اليَد, while the rare phrase أعطيته من يدي إلى يده describes handing something over. The image of transfer belongs to hands, but the verse gives no transactional scene.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N203.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ\",\"after\":\"Physical contact faintly echoes a hand-to-hand exchange.\",\"reason\":\"The rare branch describes giving يدًا بيد, hand to hand, and لَٰمَسْتُمُ means touch by hand or skin. Both involve bodily contact, though the verse’s touch is not an exchange.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N203.7\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"نِعْمَتَهُۥ\",\"after\":\"God’s favor sounds like a gift beyond any cash exchange.\",\"reason\":\"The rare hand-sense includes عن يد نقدا, payment in cash, and a sale settled hand to hand; نِعْمَتَهُۥ is freely bestowed favor. Their contrast makes the completed blessing sound gracious rather than purchased.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N203.8\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"تَشْكُرُونَ\",\"after\":\"Gratitude becomes the fitting return for a gift received.\",\"reason\":\"The rare phrase ياديت فلانا describes giving back hand for hand, while تَشْكُرُونَ is recognizing a blessing and responding to its giver. The ayah’s final thanks answers the favor without turning it into a sale.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N204\",\"lines\":\"r-r-n-n-nr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N204.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"قُمْتُمْ\",\"after\":\"The rise toward prayer becomes the threshold immediately ahead of it.\",\"reason\":\"قُمْتُمْ means rising toward prayer, while بين يدي الشيء marks what lies in front of it or immediately before it. The rare temporal image makes the rising and its cleansing acts the moment just ahead of prayer.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N204.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"Hands and faces share a frontward axis in the rite.\",\"reason\":\"The rare phrase بين يديك means what is in front of you, and وُجُوهَكُمْ names the face and the forward-facing side. Their spatial senses meet as the ayah prepares the body for prayer.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N204.5\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱمْسَحُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Wiping occupies a moment before the prayer it prepares for.\",\"reason\":\"The rare hand-image can mean what comes immediately before an event, and وَٱمْسَحُوا۟ names a preparatory wiping act. The sequence fits, though any ritual preparation could occupy that prior slot.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N204.7\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"after\":\"Coming can be heard as movement into what lies ahead.\",\"reason\":\"جَآءَ means coming or occurring, while بين يدي something describes what is ahead of it. Arrival and preceding position touch as a thin image of approach.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N204.9\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱمْسَحُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The earth-wipe also sits just before the prayer it enables.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense is what comes before a thing, and فَٱمْسَحُوا۟ names the wiping step in the substitute rite. It belongs to the prayer’s preparation, though the temporal link is general.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N204.10\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"بِوُجُوهِكُمْ\",\"after\":\"In the earth rite, the hands and face occupy one forward-facing plane.\",\"reason\":\"بين يديك means in front of you, while بِوُجُوهِكُمْ names the face, the body’s forward-facing surface. Wiping the face with the hands makes that shared spatial image concrete.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N205\",\"lines\":\"-r-nnrnn-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N205.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The hands being cleansed are also the hands that act and earn.\",\"reason\":\"The target وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ is the bodily hand, while ما كسبت اليدان means what the hands have done or earned. The rite touches the same organs that the idiom makes answerable for a person’s deeds.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N205.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱمْسَحُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Wiping is one deed performed by the hands.\",\"reason\":\"The rare phrase ما كسبت اليدان means what the hands have earned, and وَٱمْسَحُوا۟ is an act of passing the hand over something. The action fits that broad category of hand-deeds, but adds little beyond it.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N205.5\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The hand’s deeds sit beside walking performed by the feet.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense ما كسبت اليدان assigns deeds to the hands, while وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ is glossed through walking on feet. Both evoke bodily action and agency, a real but general pairing.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N205.6\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ\",\"after\":\"The touch that triggers the concession is one of the body’s acts.\",\"reason\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ means tactile contact, while ما كسبت اليدان names what the hands have done or earned. The contact is a concrete deed of the embodied agent that precedes purification.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N205.7\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"طَيِّبًا\",\"after\":\"The hands’ deeds faintly echo the wholesome surface chosen for purification.\",\"reason\":\"The rare phrase ما كسبت اليدان concerns a person’s deeds, and طَيِّبًا describes a good, clean, wholesome surface. Moral action and ritual cleanliness share an image of goodness, but the link is broad.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N205.8\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱمْسَحُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The substitute wipe is another act done by the hands.\",\"reason\":\"ما كسبت اليدان means the hands’ earned deeds, and فَٱمْسَحُوا۟ commands a physical wiping motion. That motion is one instance of hand-action, though the connection is generic.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N206\",\"lines\":\"nrrnrr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N206.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The body’s hand is itself an extension of the person.\",\"reason\":\"The target is the bodily hand, while يد الشيء can name an object’s handle, tip, or projecting extension. The physical hand fits that part-of-a-whole image, though the echo is close to the plain word.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N206.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱمْسَحُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The hand’s reach becomes the instrument that carries out the wipe.\",\"reason\":\"The rare يد الشيء is an object’s handle or extension, and وَٱمْسَحُوا۟ means passing the hand across a surface. In this command the bodily extension is precisely the tool of the action.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N206.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"بِرُءُوسِكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The projecting hand reaches the body’s summit.\",\"reason\":\"يد الشيء can mean its projecting end, while رُءُوسِكُمْ names the head and the uppermost part. The wiping sequence puts that extended limb against the body’s summit.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N206.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The hand and foot appear as bodily extensions at opposite ends.\",\"reason\":\"The rare يد الشيء is a projecting extension, and وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ is glossed through walking on feet. Both evoke limbs that extend the body into action, a thin anatomical image.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N206.5\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ\",\"after\":\"The hand’s extension is the means by which touch reaches its object.\",\"reason\":\"A rare يد الشيء is a handle or projecting end, and لَٰمَسْتُمُ means perceiving by hand or skin contact. The touch depends on that bodily extension to meet what is touched.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N206.6\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱمْسَحُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The hand’s reach carries the earth-wipe to the face.\",\"reason\":\"The rare branch calls the handle or extremity يد الشيء, and فَٱمْسَحُوا۟ commands wiping by hand. In the substitute rite, the extended hand is the tool that connects the selected surface to the body.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N207\",\"lines\":\"--r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N207.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"نِعْمَتَهُۥ\",\"after\":\"The favor is heard as roomy, comfortable abundance.\",\"reason\":\"The rare يدي means wide and spacious, as in عيش يدي واسع, while نِعْمَتَهُۥ is favor and a good condition of life. The shared sense of ease lets the blessing feel like room to live well.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N208\",\"lines\":\"---r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N208.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"لِيَجْعَلَ\",\"after\":\"The making of hardship is heard against the work of a skillful hand.\",\"reason\":\"A rare يدي describes someone صنّاع, skillful in making things, while لِيَجْعَلَ means to make or bring something about. The skilled hand is the agent or tool of the making named by the verb.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N209\",\"lines\":\"rr-r---r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N209.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"قُمْتُمْ\",\"after\":\"A supporting hand steadies the believer’s rise toward prayer.\",\"reason\":\"The rare اليد الناصرة is a hand of aid and support, while قُمْتُمْ means rising or resolutely undertaking an act. The supporter and the one who rises make a clear image of help enabling action.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N209.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"Separate hands being cleansed can be heard as one hand of support.\",\"reason\":\"The target names bodily hands, while المسلمون يد على من سواهم means that a community’s aid and word are one. The plural hands of the believers make a striking bodily image of shared protection.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N209.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The walking feet are heard beside the hand that supports their bearer.\",\"reason\":\"The rare اليد is help that prevents injustice and supports another, while وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ is glossed as walking on feet. Their pairing makes a concrete image of a helping hand beside a person on the move.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N209.8\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"target_ar\":\"نِعْمَتَهُۥ\",\"after\":\"The favor appears as aid and protection given to the believers.\",\"reason\":\"The rare اليد is الغياث, relief and support, while نِعْمَتَهُۥ names favor and good condition. The blessing at the ayah’s end can be heard as the protection that sustains its recipients.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N210\",\"lines\":\"nr--nr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N210.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"يُرِيدُ\",\"target_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The face’s direction can faintly suggest a direction restored.\",\"reason\":\"The rare ر د د sense is returning a thing to its place, while وُجُوهَكُمْ names the face and its forward direction. A face can be restored to an orientation, but the ayah does not state that return.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N210.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"يُرِيدُ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱطَّهَّرُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Purification sounds like a return to a clean state.\",\"reason\":\"The rare ر د د sense is رد الشيء إلى موضعه, returning something to its place or condition, and فَٱطَّهَّرُوا۟ commands full purification. Both can be heard as restoration from an altered state to one of purity.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N210.5\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"يُرِيدُ\",\"target_ar\":\"يُرِيدُ\",\"after\":\"Will is faintly heard as directed movement toward an aim.\",\"reason\":\"The rare branch means رجع الشيء, returning or going back toward something, while يُرِيدُ means willing or intending. A will can be directed toward a return, though the pairing is broad.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N210.6\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"يُرِيدُ\",\"target_ar\":\"لِيُطَهِّرَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The intended purification appears as a restoration to a clean condition.\",\"reason\":\"The rare ر د د sense describes returning something to its proper place, and لِيُطَهِّرَكُمْ names cleansing from impurity. Restoration and purification meet as a return from defilement to purity.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N211\",\"lines\":\"nrnr-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N211.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"يُرِيدُ\",\"target_ar\":\"ءَامَنُوٓا۟\",\"after\":\"The act of warding off a threat faintly answers the believers’ security.\",\"reason\":\"The rare ر د د sense is دفع الشيء ومنعه, turning something away or preventing it, while ءَامَنُوٓا۟ carries سكون القلب في أمن وثقة. Preventing harm can secure trust, but the connection is general.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N211.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"يُرِيدُ\",\"target_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The prayer-facing face is heard against a turning away from the face or course.\",\"reason\":\"The rare ر د د sense is رده عن وجهه, turning something away from its direction, while وُجُوهَكُمْ names the face and forward orientation. One sense points forward and the other deflects from that direction, an apt echo in a prayer-preparation verse.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N211.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"يُرِيدُ\",\"target_ar\":\"جُنُبًا\",\"after\":\"The state of being set aside echoes the act of keeping something away.\",\"reason\":\"The rare branch means دفع الشيء ومنعه, warding something off, while جُنُبًا is glossed as a side or region apart from the body. Both evoke separation, though they do not state the same action.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N211.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"يُرِيدُ\",\"target_ar\":\"لِيَجْعَلَ\",\"after\":\"The denied making of hardship sounds like an intention to repel it.\",\"reason\":\"The rare ر د د sense is الدفع والمنع, repelling or preventing, while لِيَجْعَلَ means to make or bring something about. With حَرَجٍ as the object, prevention stands directly against constructing constriction.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N212\",\"lines\":\"------\"}\n{\"id\":\"N213\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N214\",\"lines\":\"rnrr-r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N214.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"يُرِيدُ\",\"target_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"A face turned toward prayer is heard against turning back from faith.\",\"reason\":\"The rare ر د د branch is الردة, turning back from religion, while وُجُوهَكُمْ names the face and its direction. The body’s forward orientation gives apostasy a possible image of turning away.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N214.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"يُرِيدُ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"Walking feet faintly picture someone retracing a religious path.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense is ارتد الرجل عن دينه, turning back from one’s religion, while وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ evokes walking on feet. Feet can retrace a path, but the verse does not describe a religious departure.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N214.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"يُرِيدُ\",\"target_ar\":\"مَّرْضَىٰٓ\",\"after\":\"Bodily illness and religious apostasy both mark a departure from soundness.\",\"reason\":\"مَّرْضَىٰ is glossed as خروج عن الصحة والاعتدال, departu